+## Symbolic links
+
+Symbolic links in an archive are skipped unless the
+[--links](/flags/#links) flag is used, in which case they are shown as
+regular files with a `.rclonelink` suffix whose contents are the target
+of the symlink.
+
+```
+$ rclone lsl --links :archive:remote:dir/100files.zip
+       12 2025-10-27 14:39:20.000000000 cofofiy5jun
+        8 2025-10-27 14:39:20.000000000 xade.rclonelink
+```
+
+This is the same convention the local backend uses, so copying an
+archive to a file system which supports symbolic links recreates them.
+
+```
+$ rclone copy --links :archive:remote:dir/100files.zip /tmp/100files
+$ ls -l /tmp/100files/xade
+lrwxr-xr-x 1 user user 8 Oct 27 14:39 /tmp/100files/xade -> cofofiy5jun
+```
+
